\ndefinition whose "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"id"},{"type":"text","value":" matches and which does NOT declare\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"version"},{"type":"text","value":" (the \"unversioned default\")."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Otherwise undefined — the host decides whether to reject or\nuse a latest-version fallback."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"const v1 = createWorkflow({ id: 'pipeline', version: 'v1' }).handler(...)\nconst v2 = createWorkflow({ id: 'pipeline', version: 'v2' }).handler(...)\nconst wf = await selectWorkflowVersion([v1, v2], runId, store)\n?? v2 // default to latest for fresh starts / unrouted runs\nrunWorkflow({ workflow: wf, runId, ... })"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"type-parameters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type Parameters"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"t","children":[{"type":"text","value":"T"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"T"},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"extends"}]},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"link","href":"../type-aliases/AnyWorkflowDefinition.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"AnyWorkflowDefinition"}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"parameters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Parameters"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"versions","children":[{"type":"text","value":"versions"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"readonly "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"T"},{"type":"text","value":"[]"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"runid","children":[{"type":"text","value":"runId"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"string"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"runstore","children":[{"type":"text","value":"runStore"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../interfaces/RunStore.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"RunStore"}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"returns","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Promise"},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"T"},{"type":"text","value":" | "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"undefined"},{"type":"text","value":">"}]}],"headings":[{"id":"function-selectworkflowversion","text":"Function: selectWorkflowVersion()","level":1},{"id":"type-parameters","text":"Type Parameters","level":2},{"id":"t","text":"T","level":3},{"id":"parameters","text":"Parameters","level":2},{"id":"versions","text":"versions","level":3},{"id":"runid","text":"runId","level":3},{"id":"runstore","text":"runStore","level":3},{"id":"returns","text":"Returns","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n# Function: selectWorkflowVersion()\n\n```ts\nfunction selectWorkflowVersion<T>(\n   versions, \n   runId, \nrunStore): Promise<T | undefined>;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/workflow-core/src/registry/select-version.ts:28](https://github.com/TanStack/workflow/blob/main/packages/workflow-core/src/registry/select-version.ts#L28)\n\nPick the workflow version that a persisted run was started under.\n\nHosts running multiple versions of the same workflow side-by-side\nuse this to route resume calls to the right code path. Each\n`WorkflowDefinition` should carry a `version` field\n(`createWorkflow({ version: 'v1', ... })`); the helper compares\nthat against the `workflowVersion` field on the run's persisted\nstate.\n\nResolution order:\n  1. Exact match by `workflowId` AND `workflowVersion`.\n  2. If no `workflowVersion` is persisted (e.g., older runs from\n     before the version field existed), fall back to the FIRST\n     definition whose `id` matches and which does NOT declare\n     `version` (the \"unversioned default\").\n  3. Otherwise undefined — the host decides whether to reject or\n     use a latest-version fallback.\n\n    const v1 = createWorkflow({ id: 'pipeline', version: 'v1' }).handler(...)\n    const v2 = createWorkflow({ id: 'pipeline', version: 'v2' }).handler(...)\n    const wf = await selectWorkflowVersion([v1, v2], runId, store)\n                 ?? v2 // default to latest for fresh starts / unrouted runs\n    runWorkflow({ workflow: wf, runId, ... })\n\n## Type Parameters\n\n### T\n\n`T` *extends* [`AnyWorkflowDefinition`](../type-aliases/AnyWorkflowDefinition.md)\n\n## Parameters\n\n### versions\n\nreadonly `T`[]\n\n### runId\n\n`string`\n\n### runStore\n\n[`RunStore`](../interfaces/RunStore.md)\n\n## Returns\n\n`Promise`\\<`T` \\| `undefined`\\>\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: selectWorkflowVersion\ntitle: selectWorkflowVersion\n---\n\n# Function: selectWorkflowVersion()\n\n```ts\nfunction selectWorkflowVersion<T>(\n   versions, \n   runId, \nrunStore): Promise<T | undefined>;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/workflow-core/src/registry/select-version.ts:28](https://github.com/TanStack/workflow/blob/main/packages/workflow-core/src/registry/select-version.ts#L28)\n\nPick the workflow version that a persisted run was started under.\n\nHosts running multiple versions of the same workflow side-by-side\nuse this to route resume calls to the right code path. Each\n`WorkflowDefinition` should carry a `version` field\n(`createWorkflow({ version: 'v1', ... })`); the helper compares\nthat against the `workflowVersion` field on the run's persisted\nstate.\n\nResolution order:\n  1. Exact match by `workflowId` AND `workflowVersion`.\n  2. If no `workflowVersion` is persisted (e.g., older runs from\n     before the version field existed), fall back to the FIRST\n     definition whose `id` matches and which does NOT declare\n     `version` (the \"unversioned default\").\n  3. Otherwise undefined — the host decides whether to reject or\n     use a latest-version fallback.\n\n    const v1 = createWorkflow({ id: 'pipeline', version: 'v1' }).handler(...)\n    const v2 = createWorkflow({ id: 'pipeline', version: 'v2' }).handler(...)\n    const wf = await selectWorkflowVersion([v1, v2], runId, store)\n                 ?? v2 // default to latest for fresh starts / unrouted runs\n    runWorkflow({ workflow: wf, runId, ... })\n\n## Type Parameters\n\n### T\n\n`T` *extends* [`AnyWorkflowDefinition`](../type-aliases/AnyWorkflowDefinition.md)\n\n## Parameters\n\n### versions\n\nreadonly `T`[]\n\n### runId\n\n`string`\n\n### runStore\n\n[`RunStore`](../interfaces/RunStore.md)\n\n## Returns\n\n`Promise`\\<`T` \\| `undefined`\\>\n"}
